<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John IV, Duke of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1339–1399</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as John of Montfort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John IV, Duke of Brittany, of the House of Montfort, won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a> by defeating and killing his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-auray">Battle of Auray</a> in 1364. Recognised as duke by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerande">Guérande</a> in 1365, he balanced between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and established the Montfort dynasty, which ruled Brittany until 1488.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-iv-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="John IV, Duke of Brittany" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rs-nourse · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_V,_Duke_of_Brittany,_KG.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
